Package: phipmake2
Type: Package
Title: Fast, Memory-Bounded PhIP-Seq Peptide and Protein Summarisation
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: person("Avinash", "Karkada", email = "avikarkada@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A rewrite of the Larman Lab 'phipmake' post-alignment stage.
    Splits multi-library PhIP-Seq peptide matrices into sub-libraries, joins
    peptide annotations, and collapses peptides to proteins by sum ('prosum'),
    maximum ('promax') and independent-epitope count ('polyclonal'). Replaces
    the original per-protein R loops with single grouped 'data.table' passes and
    streams sub-library results to disk instead of holding whole-screen copies
    in memory. Output file names and layout are drop-in compatible with
    phipmake 0.2.8.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.0)
Imports:
    data.table (>= 1.14.0),
    igraph (>= 1.2.0),
    stats,
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
